{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovParameterFibreRank","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovParameterFibreRank","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.pow_two_mul_eq_one_of_zRank_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.pow_two_mul_eq_one_of_zRank_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovParameterFibreRank.lean#L93-L112","doc":"Bar-invariance of a nonzero rank-`N` Markov parameter forces\n`q^(2N) = 1`.\n\nContrapositive reading: at any `q` with `q^(2N) ≠ 1` — in particular any real\nsubstrate `q₀ > 1` at any rank `N ≥ 1` — the rank-`N` Markov parameter is\n**not** bar-invariant.  No fibre rank rescues bar-invariance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.zRank_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.zRank_bar","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovParameterFibreRank.lean#L76-L91","doc":"**Bar-covariance law.** Replacing `q` by `q⁻¹` rescales the rank-`N`\nMarkov parameter by `q^(-2N)`:\n\n`zRank N q⁻¹ = zRank N q / q^(2N)`.\n\nThe whole family is bar-*covariant* of weight `q^(-2N)`; it is bar-invariant\nonly where `q^(2N) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.zRank_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.zRank_two","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovParameterFibreRank.lean#L65-L74","doc":"Convention D is rank `2`: `zRank 2 q = q³/(q² + 1)`.\n\nThe hypotheses are exactly non-degeneracy of the rank-2 parameter: `q ≠ 0`\nand `q⁴ ≠ 1`, the latter split as `q² ≠ 1` and `q² ≠ -1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.zRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.zRank","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovParameterFibreRank.lean#L57-L63","doc":"The Markov stabilisation parameter at fibre rank `N`:\n`zRank N q = q^(2N-1)·(q² - 1)/(q^(2N) - 1)`, equivalently `qᴺ/[N]_q`.\n\nWritten as `q^(2N)·(q² - 1) / (q·(q^(2N) - 1))` to avoid natural-number\nsubtraction in the exponent. ","signatureChunk":0}]}